{"kind":"assert","text":"H5 positive-path ruling: the boundary is authorized, with one family. Add a separately versioned, strict package reader that understands groups, and a new Rules pin that selects it. Packing, the CLI reader and the install worker all use that reader. Old Rules 15 stays byte for byte, and the early older-family refusal keeps protecting it.\n\nDo not add a later family. The new Rules pin becomes the Rules sibling of the family that H3 creates, in place of Rules 15. One new family then carries both the Order pin and the reader that can install a group, so no room ever gets an Order pin it cannot install. Change H3's planned cohort the same way. My approval of the H3 family (eeba824a) stands with that one sibling changed.\n\nOrder: the reader and the Rules pin are a prerequisite commit, and the H3 head that creates the family must contain it. Land H3 and that H5 commit in one gated group, or land the H5 prerequisite first. Never land the H3 family on Rules 15.\n\nBefore you write the reader, search for an existing selector that replay already proves, for example a versioned codec chosen by the Rules pin. If one exists, use it and report it. If none exists, build the new reader as described. Record both the decision and the changed sibling in the H3 and H5 Status lines.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}